      "text": "To determine the measure of angle \\( P \\) in the given polygon, we need to use the fact that the sum of the interior angles of a polygon with \\( n \\) sides is given by the formula:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Sum of interior angles} = (n-2) \\times 180^\\circ\n\\]\n\nFirst, let's identify the number of sides of the polygon. The polygon is not a regular hexagon, but we can see that it has one interior angle that measures \\( 128^\\circ \\). The other three interior angles are given as \\( 92^\\circ \\), \\( 113^\\circ \\), and \\( 111^\\circ \\).\n\nWe need to find the measure of angle \\( P \\). Since the polygon has a total of 6 sides, it is a hexagon. The sum of the interior angles of a hexagon is:\n\n\\[\n(6-2) \\times 180^\\circ = 4 \\times 180^\\circ = 720^\\circ\n\\]\n\nWe know the measures of five of the angles:\n\\[\n128^\\circ, \\quad 92^\\circ, \\quad 113^\\circ, \\quad 111^\\circ\n\\]\n\nLet the measure of angle \\( P \\) be \\( x \\). The sum of these five angles plus angle \\( P \\) should equal \\( 720^\\circ \\). Therefore, we can write the equation:\n\n\\[\n128^\\circ + 92^\\circ + 113^\\circ + 111^\\circ + x = 720^\\circ\n\\]\n\nNow, let's calculate the sum of the known angles:\n\n\\[\n128^\\circ + 92^\\circ + 113^\\circ + 111^\\circ = 444^\\circ\n\\]\n\nSubstituting this sum back into the equation, we get:\n\n\\[\n444^\\circ + x = 720^\\circ\n\\]\n\nTo find \\( x \\), we subtract \\( 444^\\circ \\) from \\( 720^\\circ \\):\n\n\\[\nx = 720^\\circ - 444^\\circ = 276^\\circ\n\\]\n\nThus, the measure of angle \\( P \\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{276}\n\\]",
